  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nServer Sent Events are fantastic for many things however for whatever reason the `event.data` is automatically dropped when an HTTP 4xx or 5xx error is encountered. That is an explicit bug that causes a lot of issues. The server sent the correct HTTP response code however now JavaScript has to deal with a blind error.\n\nBecause `event.data` is not set I now have to program a new request to the server to request knowing what the error was in spite of the fact that I sent that error that _should_ be easily accessible via `event.data`. That also means I have to waste CPU and RAM resources holding on to an error message because of this bug.\n\nI simply don't have the time to do digging through the specification, do interpretation, etc. The specification needs to be updated to _explicitly_ require `event.data` to _always_ be accessible presuming it has been sent by the server _regardless of all other conditions_.",
